<title>USA: American International Q4 shr rises. [CORRECTED 15:32 GMT]</title>
<headline>American International Q4 shr rises. [CORRECTED 15:32 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Oper shr		    $1.61		    $1.40</p>
<p> Oper net		  759,900		  661,800</p>
<p>(Corrects operating net for both periods)</p>
<p> Revs		    7,420,000		6,860,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  469,468		  474,130</p>
<p>			TWELVE MONTHS</p>
<p> Oper shr		    $6.03		    $5.20</p>
<p> Oper net		2,841,900		2,465,200</p>
<p> Revs		   28,210,000	     25,870,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  471,000		  474,000</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Net income per share was $770.2 million, or $1.64 a share, in the 1996 Q4 compared to $673.8 million, or $1.43 a share in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Net income for 1996 was $2.90 billion, or $6.15 a share compared with $2.51 billion, or $5.30 a share in 1995.</p>
<p>Operating income excludes realized capital gains, net of taxes.</p>
